  249                                   new_offset:                             ; Java: beginMatchFromNewOffset/readOffset
  250                                   ; Two class bits: the first says byte or word, the second picks a byte offset's
  251                                   ; 256-unit bank or, for a word, marks the end of the stream. That first bit is
  252                                   ; the only read here that can need a refill. Every operation is an even number
  253                                   ; of bits, so flags and gamma data bits all land on odd positions and the queue
  254                                   ; - which empties every 16 bits - can never run out on one; the bit immediately
  255                                   ; after a flag is the one exception, and it is checked.
